# No em dashes

Do not use the Unicode em dash (`—`, U+2014) anywhere in this project.

This covers all **customer-facing** text: page copy, headings, buttons, labels, form messages, metadata descriptions, alt text, product and pattern blurbs in `src/data/`, and any other string shown on the site.

Also avoid em dashes in **new** repo prose (docs, skills, rules, comments) when you write or edit those files.

## Use instead

- Two sentences: period, then the next thought.
- A comma or colon when a short pause is enough.
- Parentheses for a quick aside.
- A middle dot (`·`) only when the design already uses it for separators (e.g. cart line details).

## Examples

- Good: "Local pickup only. Venmo when we meet."
- Bad: "Local pickup only — Venmo when we meet."
- Good: "Free pattern: link coming once Diana confirms the source."
- Bad: "Free pattern — link coming once Diana confirms the source."

Do not substitute `--` or `–` (en dash) where an em dash would go in copy. Rephrase with plain punctuation.
